course: dictionary
lesson: 11941
title: Words from church and choir
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one special place, such as church or a choir. You may not hear them at school or at home, but the words around them can still help. «The choir sang a canticle before the prayers were read.» A choir sings, and the sentence says the canticle was sung, so a canticle must be a kind of song.
explain: Look for clues that tell you what kind of thing a word is. «The Magnificat is a canticle, a song of praise taken from the Bible.» The words «song of praise» and «taken from the Bible» tell you what a canticle is. Canticle is a noun, a naming word for a thing.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. «We sing canticles at evening prayer.» If you swap in «songs with words from the Bible», the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: A canticle is a song or hymn with words from the Bible.
fact: Canticles are sung in church services, such as morning and evening prayer.
fact: «The Magnificat» is a famous canticle, and it is sometimes called the canticle of Mary.
fact: «Canticle» can also mean a song of praise, even when it is not sung in church.
fact: You can say «sing the canticles» when you mean singing these songs in a service.
exercise: «The choir sang a canticle before the prayers.» What is a canticle? | A kind of church bell | A quiet prayer said in silence | *A song or hymn with words from the Bible | A long walk to the church
exercise: «At evening prayer, the church sang a canticle of praise.» What does canticle mean here? | A quiet pause for thinking | A bag for holding books | *A song of praise | A type of candle
exercise: «Canticles are sung in church services.» Which words tell you where canticles are sung? | sung | in the | *church services | canticles are
test: «The Magnificat is a famous canticle.» What is the best meaning? | A school test | A famous painting | *A song with words from the Bible | A kind of cake
test: «The choir learned the canticle of Mary.» What does the phrase «the canticle of Mary» mean? | A story about a dog | *A song of praise about Mary, sung in church | A quiet walk in the woods | A map of a town
exam: Which sentence uses canticle the way a dictionary describes it? | «The canticle ran fast across the field.» | «He drew a canticle on the wall.» | *«The congregation sang a canticle with words from the Bible.» | «The canticle was a sandwich eaten at lunch.»
